WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.394 --> 00:00:02.402
-Hey, guys, I´m here
with Blake Shelton,

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:03.603
the one and only.
We´re at Nobu.

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:05.271
And Blake,
I can´t believe this is true,

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:08.675
but you´ve never tried
sushi before.

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:12.278
-I mean, not the raw --
like, the raw stuff, no.

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:17.117
♫♫

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:19.119
Don´t eat this.
This is a hot towel.

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:20.687
It´s not a sushi roll.

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:23.656
So you clean your hands
with this.

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:25.692
See?
-Ah.

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:27.894
-That´s how you
clean your hands?

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:30.163
-♫ La-la-la-la-la-la-la-la-la ♫

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:31.998
-Have you ever had sake before?

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:33.633
This is -- this is delicious.

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:36.569
It´s a wine.
It´s a rice wine.

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:37.937
What´s -- are you getting
a headache?

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:40.807
-No, I just -- I don´t know
what -- rice wine.

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:43.710
-Yeah. Not "race wane."
Rice. Rice wine.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.479
-What did you call it?
-Rice.

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:49.382
You ever had rice before?
Thank you.

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:52.619
Here´s to best friends.
Tonight is kind of special.

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:54.721
-Why are you doing this?
-´Cause I love you. That´s all.

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:57.157
We´re gonna have fun.
This is good. Cheers.

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:01.828
What does it tastes like to you?
-Easter egg coloring.

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:04.864
-Easter egg coloring.
-Does it to you, too?

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:06.366
-Have you tried
the fresh ginger?

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:08.268
It´s pickled ginger.

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:10.437
-I wouldn´t know
fresh ginger from old.

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:15.875
-What do you think about this?

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:20.547
-Kind of has the texture
of pre-chewed gum.

00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:22.482
-Can we get the next course,
please?

00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:26.219
♫♫

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:27.220
Blake, don´t -- don´t --
-Oh, my God.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:28.855
-No. Don´t be freaked out.

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:30.590
Look at how colorful,
look how beautiful.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:31.858
Thank you very much.

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:33.693
You should thank them
when they --

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:35.095
-Thank you!
-Now it´s too late.

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:36.362
-Thank you!
-That´s right, Blake.

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:38.231
-Can we get some more rice wine?

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:41.334
-Which one you wanna go with?
The tuna or the salmon?

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:43.770
-Does it matter?
-Yeah, I think so.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:46.039
-I don´t know the difference.

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:49.175
That right there it looks like
a human tongue.

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:53.680
♫♫

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:56.416
The texture is...

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:59.319
Play-Doh.

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:02.122
But I will say this
to you right now...

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:04.958
-Yeah.
-...man to man.

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:07.327
-Thank you.
-I like that.

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:08.962
I like how that tasted, but --

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:10.330
-There´s one. Count one.
That´s one.

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:11.831
-Okay, that´s one.

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:14.134
So what is this?
-This is yellowtail.

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:16.202
Try it in the soy sauce
and then just take half of it.

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:17.770
This is good.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.873
[ Chuckles ]

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:24.043
-I don´t like that.
-Oh, come on.

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:25.845
-I don´t like that.

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:28.448
♫♫

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:32.652
Hey, what could be more
disgusting than raw fish?

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:34.854
Whatever this is.
No, I don´t want to toast.

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:37.590
-No, I know. I´m sorry.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:38.758
-Whole thing, huh?

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:42.896
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:47.066
-Can we get some more
of that rice wine?

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:50.403
♫♫

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:52.605
But can you at least tell me
what this is?

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:54.107
-Honestly, I´m not kidding,
I´m just --

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:56.009
-You don´t know, okay.

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:57.443
Just shut up.

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:58.545
-It´s a fish.
I can look at it.

00:02:58.545 --> 00:02:59.779
-Stop talking.
-It´s a little fish head.

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:00.880
You see the --
-Stop talking.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.115
-Little fish head.
Do you see it?

00:03:02.115 --> 00:03:03.283
-I´m not looking.
I don´t want to know

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:04.751
-Look at him.
-It´s already in my mouth.

00:03:04.751 --> 00:03:05.752
-What´s the name
of the new record,

00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:08.855
just so I can plug
the record quick?

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:10.957
"Free Popcorn Shrimp"?
Something like that?

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:13.960
-"Free Popcorn Shrimp."
-"Free Popcorn Shrimp."

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:15.261
No, seriously,
what´s the name of it?

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:16.696
It´s called, like,
"This Bar Ain´t Good Enough"?

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:20.633
-Yes.
-♫ This bar ain´t good enough ♫

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:23.102
♫ Bar used to be real tough ♫

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:26.206
-See?
-♫ Bar used to be real rough ♫

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:28.508
♫ Now the bar
ain´t tough enough ♫

00:03:28.508 --> 00:03:30.443
-Hey, can we get some rice wine?

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:33.479
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:36.950
-Hey, man, what´s real?

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:38.651
You seen Jimmy around here,
my friend?

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:40.253
About 4-foot-9.

00:03:40.253 --> 00:03:41.688
A weird look on his face.

00:03:41.688 --> 00:03:43.356
Had a lot of rice wine.

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:47.360
Check this out.

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:49.963
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.963 --> 00:03:51.564
Merry Christmas, bitch.

00:03:51.564 --> 00:03:53.433
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:55.802
♫♫

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:57.036
Ready?

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:58.638
Boom! Go for it.

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:04.611
-Oh, my God. It pulled --

00:04:04.611 --> 00:04:05.745
No!

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:08.414
-What is this?

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:10.483
-It´s a sea urchin uni shot.

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:12.952
-I´m sorry?
-Uni. Sea urchin.

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:15.421
-Sea urchin.
-Gonads of the sea urchin.

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:17.657
-Gonads.
-Gonads...

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:19.859
-Sea urchin.

00:04:19.859 --> 00:04:23.229
-But you -- you said gonads.

00:04:23.229 --> 00:04:24.897
Hey, can we get some
rice wine?

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:26.499
-What are you gonna do?
Are you gonna chew it

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:27.734
or just swallow
the whole thing down?

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:29.669
-I´m gonna pretend
like this isn´t happening.

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:30.937
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.937 --> 00:04:33.139
-Hey, what´s the name
of the new single?

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:35.742
-"Came Here to Forget."

00:04:35.742 --> 00:04:38.211
-[ Laughing ]
Mission accomplished.

00:04:38.211 --> 00:04:41.114
I can´t. I can´t do it.
I can´t do it.

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:43.416
[ Audience gasping
and cheering ]

00:04:47.453 --> 00:04:50.356
-I did it.

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:52.592
Come on. You don´t want
to be that guy.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:58.064
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.064 --> 00:05:00.767
-Oh, my God!

00:05:00.767 --> 00:05:04.037
-Ugh! Oh, my gosh.
That was delicious.

00:05:04.037 --> 00:05:05.605
-How about a high-five?
-Thank you so much.

00:05:06.539 --> 00:05:09.642
♫♫

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:13.413
All right, Blake,
we got the last course for you.

00:05:13.413 --> 00:05:14.914
Had all different kinds
of sushi.

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:17.183
This last one is gonna
blow your mind.

00:05:22.155 --> 00:05:23.289
-What?!

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:25.525
-You earned it, buddy.

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:28.895
Big Mac.
-Oh, my gosh!

00:05:28.895 --> 00:05:30.797
Now we´re talking!
-I love you, man.

00:05:30.797 --> 00:05:32.465
-Yes!
-Two more rice wines.

00:05:32.465 --> 00:05:34.067
-I love it!
Can we get some more rice win?

00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:36.035
-Blake Shelton, everybody.
[ Laughs ]

00:05:36.035 --> 00:05:38.071
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:40.173
´Cause I do love you.
I´m a big fan of yours.

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:41.774
-I love you, too, Jimmy.
-Oh, come on.

00:05:41.774 --> 00:05:42.875
I didn´t believe that at all.

00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:44.711
-You don´t?
-What´s my last name?

00:05:44.711 --> 00:05:46.846
-It´s..."Fallen."

00:05:46.846 --> 00:05:47.847
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.847 --> 00:05:49.449
-Hey, I want to
congratulate you.

00:05:49.449 --> 00:05:52.418
This morning you were nominated
for three CMA Awards.

00:05:52.418 --> 00:05:53.653
-Thank you.
-Three.

00:05:53.653 --> 00:05:56.222
-Thank you.
-One, two, three.

00:05:56.222 --> 00:05:58.358
That´s big.
Entertainer of the year,

00:05:58.358 --> 00:06:00.893
male vocalist,
and single of the year.

00:06:00.893 --> 00:06:02.295
-[ Laughs ] I´m sorry.
-What?

00:06:02.295 --> 00:06:04.697
-Just, no matter what the moment
is, it´s, ♫ Dunnn ♫

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:06.833
-Yeah.
[ Music sting plays ]

00:06:06.833 --> 00:06:08.534
-That´s great.
-You can´t be --

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:10.837
-I wish that was in my house,
man, just...

00:06:10.837 --> 00:06:13.573
-You´re like, "Honey, I´m gonna
watch a movie on Lifetime."

00:06:13.573 --> 00:06:16.008
[ Music sting plays ]

00:06:16.008 --> 00:06:17.310
Yeah, that´s the way it works.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:18.745
-Oh, I´m listening to you.
I´m sorry. Go ahead.

00:06:18.745 --> 00:06:20.213
There´s a lot of distractions
here.

00:06:20.213 --> 00:06:22.915
-I know. I´m sorry.
But I´m very distracted as well.

00:06:22.915 --> 00:06:24.650
-Okay.
-Actually, I started a --

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.486
I have a truck.
I bought a truck.

00:06:26.486 --> 00:06:28.221
And I started a truck --
-Man, I heard about that.

00:06:28.221 --> 00:06:29.956
-Thank you. Yeah,
and I´m very excited about it.

00:06:29.956 --> 00:06:32.492
-What did you get?
-I got a Ford F-150 King Ranch.

00:06:32.492 --> 00:06:35.661
-Yes. My wife, Miranda,
has that same truck,

00:06:35.661 --> 00:06:37.430
and it´s a diesel.

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:39.966
[ Laughter ]

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:47.874
-Men and women can both enjoy
the same truck.

00:06:47.874 --> 00:06:49.475
-Sure, they can. It´s --
-Yeah, absolutely.

00:06:49.475 --> 00:06:51.644
-It´s 2014. Of course they can.
-It certainly is.

00:06:51.644 --> 00:06:54.881
-It´s cool these days.
-It is cool, always.

00:06:54.881 --> 00:06:58.050
And I got a truck,
and so I wanted a --

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:02.088
I wanted a truck playlist,
a good country truck playlist.

00:07:02.088 --> 00:07:04.657
And so I asked everyone
watching "The Tonight Show"

00:07:04.657 --> 00:07:05.758
to send in their favorite songs,

00:07:05.758 --> 00:07:07.226
and I added
some of my favorite songs.

00:07:07.226 --> 00:07:08.795
And you´re actually
on my playlist twice --

00:07:08.795 --> 00:07:10.530
two of your songs.
I´m a big fan.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:12.398
-Okay, wait a minute, though.
-Yeah.

00:07:12.398 --> 00:07:14.267
You´re on my truck --
you´re in my truck.

00:07:14.267 --> 00:07:16.903
-No, no, no, no. Did the --

00:07:16.903 --> 00:07:19.772
-♫ You´re in my truck,
you´re in my ♫

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:21.174
-Stop.
-Sorry.

00:07:21.174 --> 00:07:23.743
[ Laughter ]

00:07:23.743 --> 00:07:26.646
-Now, are my songs on your
playlist as the ones you added.

00:07:26.646 --> 00:07:28.448
Are they on your playlist
as the ones

00:07:28.448 --> 00:07:31.851
that people advised you to add?
Be honest.

00:07:31.851 --> 00:07:34.253
-It doesn´t matter, Blake.
It doesn´t matter.

00:07:34.253 --> 00:07:35.955
-All right, you answered.
Go ahead.

00:07:35.955 --> 00:07:37.557
-No, I do --
-Let me ask you.

00:07:37.557 --> 00:07:40.159
Okay, let --
How´s the truck looking?

00:07:40.159 --> 00:07:41.561
-It´s gorgeous.
-How long have you had it now?

00:07:41.561 --> 00:07:43.763
-It´s blue -- the top is blue
and the bottom´s khaki.

00:07:43.763 --> 00:07:45.565
It looks like
it works at Best Buy.

00:07:45.565 --> 00:07:47.467
It has, like, a blue --

00:07:47.467 --> 00:07:49.902
like, a blue golf-shirt top
and khaki bottoms.

00:07:49.902 --> 00:07:51.604
-Have you been using it?

00:07:51.604 --> 00:07:52.939
-Oh, yeah, I´m driving
all over the place.

00:07:52.939 --> 00:07:54.974
I´m just a truck-driving dude.

00:07:54.974 --> 00:07:56.776
Look at me. Look at me.
Don´t I look like a guy --

00:07:56.776 --> 00:07:58.744
-You keeping it clean?
Is it looking nice?

00:07:58.744 --> 00:08:01.814
-It´s pretty clean, yeah.
-That´s wrong.

00:08:01.814 --> 00:08:03.282
What are talking about?

00:08:03.282 --> 00:08:05.551
Blake, I just had to -- well,
it´s a very expensive truck.

00:08:05.551 --> 00:08:08.221
-If you´re gonna buy a...

00:08:08.221 --> 00:08:10.756
a truck...
[ Laughter ]

00:08:10.756 --> 00:08:11.924
-It´s a beautiful truck.

00:08:11.924 --> 00:08:13.593
-...you gotta get
some mud on it.

00:08:13.593 --> 00:08:15.495
You gotta have mud on the side.
You got to have dents in it,

00:08:15.495 --> 00:08:17.163
scratches, guts in the back.

00:08:17.163 --> 00:08:20.733
-Really?
-Yeah, corn and shovels and...

00:08:20.733 --> 00:08:22.435
-Corn and shovels?
-Just, you know --

00:08:22.435 --> 00:08:24.370
-It sounds like
a "Dateline" episode.

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:27.640
Guts? It sounds like Lester Holt
to be doing this.

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:29.308
-Just crap, you know?
-Really?

00:08:29.308 --> 00:08:30.576
-You gotta have -- yes.

00:08:30.576 --> 00:08:32.979
-I´ll do it.
-Trucks are a tool.

00:08:32.979 --> 00:08:36.048
You don´t drive
around the city in it.

00:08:36.048 --> 00:08:38.050
-No, I know.
It´s not a city truck.

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:40.953
It´s a country truck.
Put things in the back that --

00:08:40.953 --> 00:08:44.790
-Well, where does it live?
-In the country.

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:47.226
It´s on, like, a farm
out in the country.

00:08:47.226 --> 00:08:50.162
-Okay.
-It´s in rehab right now.

00:08:50.162 --> 00:08:51.597
-Is it? [ Laughs ]

00:08:51.597 --> 00:08:53.499
-My truck´s in rehab, yeah.
-Cool.

00:08:53.499 --> 00:08:54.934
-No, I got -- you can
put things in the back.

00:08:54.934 --> 00:08:56.402
I got it because --
it´s very important --

00:08:56.402 --> 00:08:58.371
it´s pumpkin season coming up,

00:08:58.371 --> 00:09:03.042
and I´m gonna want places
to put the pumpkins

00:09:03.042 --> 00:09:04.644
when you drive --
-Of course.

00:09:04.644 --> 00:09:06.512
I don´t know why
I didn´t think of that.

00:09:06.512 --> 00:09:09.582
It is getting close
to pumpkin season,

00:09:09.582 --> 00:09:11.884
and gotta go get a load of them.

00:09:11.884 --> 00:09:13.920
-That´s -- [ Laughs ]

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:16.489
Hey, guys. I´m here with my pal
Blake Shelton.

00:09:16.489 --> 00:09:18.925
We´re at Riverdale Stables
here in New York.

00:09:18.925 --> 00:09:20.493
Now, Blake, the last time
you were on the show,

00:09:20.493 --> 00:09:22.128
I made you do something
you´ve never done before --

00:09:22.128 --> 00:09:23.729
try sushi.

00:09:25.965 --> 00:09:27.667
-Oh, my God. It pulled --

00:09:27.667 --> 00:09:28.801
No!

00:09:28.801 --> 00:09:31.270
Can we get some more rice wine?

00:09:31.270 --> 00:09:34.173
Yes. I´m still having
nightmares about that.

00:09:34.173 --> 00:09:35.775
-Well, being the nice guy
that I am,

00:09:35.775 --> 00:09:38.544
I thought I´d give you
a chance for some payback.

00:09:38.544 --> 00:09:39.745
Now you´re gonna make me
do something

00:09:39.745 --> 00:09:42.014
I´ve never done before...
-[ Laughs evilly ]

00:09:42.014 --> 00:09:43.849
-...milk a cow.
-Can´t wait.

00:09:43.849 --> 00:09:45.518
I can´t wait for this!

00:09:45.518 --> 00:09:48.788
[ Banjo music playing ]

00:09:49.722 --> 00:09:52.825
Okay, Jimmy. This is Oreo.

00:09:52.825 --> 00:09:54.727
-Okay, cool.
-Meet Oreo.

00:09:54.727 --> 00:09:57.096
-Hi, Oreo.
Did I overdress?

00:09:57.096 --> 00:09:58.598
Because I thought...

00:09:58.598 --> 00:10:00.733
-You dressed very disrespectful.

00:10:00.733 --> 00:10:02.802
You look like Howdy Doody
right now.

00:10:02.802 --> 00:10:04.303
Do you think this is a game?

00:10:04.303 --> 00:10:07.039
You think this is a game?
This is serious.

00:10:07.039 --> 00:10:08.574
-[ Laughing ] Oh, my gosh.

00:10:08.574 --> 00:10:09.942
I just dressed for the part.

00:10:09.942 --> 00:10:11.777
And this is, like,
